.env
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
coverage.xml
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
.DS_Store
*.sqlite3
media/
staticfiles/
evidence/
# An `EVIDENCE_ROOT` a developer points inside the checkout while running the
# browser suite locally. `evidence/` above does not cover a dotted name, and the
# blob store writes real-looking filenames the moment the suite captures
# anything — synthetic here, but the store is the one place this repository must
# never accumulate files by accident (docs/adr/0047 round; the orphan-evidence
# leak this pattern is named after).
.e2e-evidence/
.uv/

# Real source material and import output never enter Git.
# The repository is public; even were it private, real row-level data and the
# reports derived from it belong in local storage only (Stage-2A brief 3).
private-data/
import-input/
import-output/
#
# Stage 2H writes its reconciliation reports here. The aggregate summary is
# publishable; the row-level one names matters, ministries and filenames, so
# the whole directory is ignored rather than the operator being asked to
# remember which file is which (Stage-2H brief 50).
.local/
opinion-archive/
#
# No workbook is ever committed, not even a synthetic one: the synthetic
# fixtures are generated by the tests that use them, so a checked-in .xlsx
# could only be a real one that arrived by accident.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls

# Written into the image at build time; never source files. GIT_SHA carries the
# commit the image was built from, so a stale copy in a checkout would describe
# the wrong build (docs/adr/0021).
BUILD_STAMP
GIT_SHA

# The Stage-2D historical corpus and everything derived from it. The archive is
# 4.14 GiB of members' legal work; a page's own XML and its derived text are the
# same material in a smaller file.
onenote-desktop-archive/
onenote-juristid-export/
migration-audit/
historical-source/
legacy-source/
derivatives/
*.tsv
!tests/**/*.tsv

# Host-side secrets. The shared gate password, the tunnel credential and the
# server's environment file exist on the server and nowhere else (docs/adr/0016).
*.env
juristid.env
cloudflared/
cert.pem
*credentials*.json

# Database dumps.
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.dump

# Screenshots and browser artefacts. A screenshot of the real deployment is real
# data in an image, which no reviewer of a diff would think to look at.
artifacts/
*.png
!static/**/*.png
# The visual-regression baselines are the exception, and the reason the rule
# exists does not reach them: they can only be produced by the browser job,
# which runs with REAL_DATA_ALLOWED=0 against `seed_e2e_data` — a command that
# refuses to run anywhere real data is permitted. Every pixel in them is
# synthetic, and a baseline that is not in the repository is not a baseline.
!e2e/baselines/*.png
